<title>USA: W.House's Raines says no US budget deal at moment.</title>
<headline>W.House's Raines says no US budget deal at moment.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House Budget Director Franklin Raines said on Tuesday there was no budget deal with Congressional leaders at the moment, and getting one in 24 hours would be &quot;remarkable.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;There's no deal at the moment, and it would be remarkable progress if there was one in 24 hours,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>Senate Majority Leader Trent Lott had said earlier that he saw an opportunity to conclude a budget agreement with the White House and Democrats within 24 hours.</p>
</text>
